Package: snpscaper
Type: Package
Title: Explore Human Genetic Variation with 1000 Genomes Project Data
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jarek", "Bryk", email = "j.bryk@hud.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2791-9709")),
    person("Alexander", "Marshall", email = "amarshall131299@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: A teaching package for exploring variation in human populations. 
    It fetches genotypes for any genomic region directly from the 1000 Genomes Project, 
    prepares them for analysis, and supports principal component analysis,
    admixture analysis, allele frequencies, Fst, heterozygosity and linkage disequilibrium, 
    with ready-made plots and an HTML handout report. 
    The entire workflow is done in R, with no command line or other external dependencies. 
    This project was first proposed by me and completed by my project student, Alex Marshall, in 2023. 
    Claude took our messy code, added R-based extraction of genotypes from the 1kgp 
    and refactored the code into a standalone package.
